  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">YR2OF2 PYMT FOR PROJECT &apos;IMPROVING MOBILE PASTORAL ACCESS TO COMPREHENSIVE AND</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the current IMPACTS I project, HPA plans to expand to two more communities Lafey sub-county (Kenya), scaling up and/or adapting proven approaches to ensuring government SRH services are culturally appropriate, accessible to all, and integrate GBV and FGM. Innovative approaches such as community scorecards and mobile phone-based feedback systems will put the pastoralist women at the forefront of influencing change at community and health system level resulting into improved sexual and reproductive health and rights for 19,195 Kenyan and 23,154 Ethiopian minority pastoralist women of reproductive health age in support of SDG 3.</narrative>
  </description>
